From fbc6016dfc870eab1b8e559814595d1a08ae75c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:50:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] feat: deliver alerts to HarmonyOS devices through
 Huawei Push Kit

A HarmonyOS device can only be reached while its app is not running through
Push Kit. The daemon gains a huawei push provider that sends notification
messages through Push Kit's v3 API, authenticated with a service account
JWT (PS256). It is available on a host whose PASEO_HOME/huawei-push holds the
service-account.json AppGallery Connect issues; options.json there sets the
message category and whether to send test messages, which is what works
before the app holds the notification self-classification entitlement.

A tap carries the alert data under paseoNotificationData, the want parameter
the HarmonyOS shell already routes for its local notifications. Tokens Push
Kit reports as invalid are revoked.

The client can name a provider when it registers or revokes a token, and the
HarmonyOS build registers its Push Kit token with every host that lists
huawei in pushProviders.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
